{"reference":"Genesis 15","book":"Genesis","chapter":15,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Abraham's seed and promise","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Galatians concludes that those belonging to Messiah are Abraham's seed and heirs according to promise, drawing inheritance into its sustained rereading of Genesis. The supplied context also prevents Roman household law from becoming the sole source for the chapter's heir and kinship language; this is a disputed reception-history claim.","verse_refs":["Genesis 15:1-6"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_genesis_015_1be981fe6a793d8888511fd1"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}
